  "all_ingredients_flat": "besan (chickpea flour), jowar flour (sorghum flour), carrot, zucchini, red onion, cilantro, jeera (cumin seeds), ajwain (carom seeds), paprika, methi leaves, Garam Masala, turmeric powder, black pepper powder, Tofu, Sprouts",
  "instructions": "BATTER\n+ Combine besan (chickpea flour) & jowar flour (sorghum flour) in 1:1 ratio.\n+ Add shredded or finely minced vegetables of our choice (carrot, zucchini, red onion, ...).\n+ Add herbs & spices like cilantro, jeera (cumin seeds), ajwain (carom seeds), paprika, methi leaves, Garam Masala, turmeric powder, black pepper powder \u2014 adjust the ratios of these spices per taste. See first pic on the left.\n+ Mix well, making sure that the batter is a little thinner than pancake batter and easily spreadable on a non-stick pan.\n+ Spread the batter on a non-stick pan. Roast for a few minutes on medium heat. Then flip over and roast the other side too.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "no-cook",
    "roast"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Serve with chutneys of your choice or with stuffing of your choice (pic shows Scrambled Tofu & Sprouts).",
